WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.000
Twelve minutes. Two ways to begin.
One person presses play; the other starts in silence.

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:14.000
Both complete the same small task.
What did the work—the sound, or the decision to start?

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:21.000
Research on auditory stimulation finds mixed results.

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:28.000
Brainwave entrainment is not an established shortcut
to reliable cognitive improvement.

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:35.000
An enjoyable listening experience is not the same as
a scientifically proven cognitive benefit.

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:42.000
Try a simple task, then examine the product, cost,
evidence and return terms. You may not need to buy.
